% FROOT Lab publications.
%
% This file is the single source for publications.html: the page reads it in
% the browser (assets/js/publications.js) and renders one entry per record,
% grouped by year, newest first. Within a year, entries keep the order they
% have in this file, so put the most important ones first.
%
% Standard BibTeX fields used:
%   title, author (separated by " and "), year, booktitle (for @inproceedings),
%   journal (for @article), url (link shown as "Paper").
% Extra fields understood by the renderer:
%   venue  = short display name for the venue, e.g. {USENIX NSDI}. If absent,
%            booktitle/journal is shown. Conference venues get a 'YY suffix.
%   code   = URL shown as "Code".
%   note   = short status text appended to the venue line, e.g. {To appear}.
%   award  = shown on its own line in bold, e.g. {Best Paper Award}.
% The citation key becomes the entry's HTML id, so index.html can link to
% publications.html#r2cc.

